                <p>in the mdc part, <rend fontstyle="italic">Qui habitat</rend> and the remaining movements are probably in the hand of Leysser; all remaining parts by Ristl</p>
                <p>This manuscript combines six works into a completorium: <rend fontstyle="italic">Cum invocarem</rend> TumW D.2.5, <rend fontstyle="italic">In te Domine speravi</rend> TumW D.2.12, <rend fontstyle="italic">Qui habitat in adiutorio</rend> TumW D.2.23, <rend fontstyle="italic">Ecce nunc benedicite</rend> TumW D.2.11, <rend fontstyle="italic">Te lucis ante terminum</rend> TumW C.2.5, and <rend fontstyle="italic">Nunc dimittis</rend> TumW D.4.4.</p>
